On 26 Jun 2006 07:57:13 -0700, Doug Freyburger wrote:

>Rachel Elizabeth Dillon wrote:

>When I play wizards I waffle between mostly throwing daggers and
>mostly casting spells for much of the game, and then below the
>Castle there isn't enough space for either any more and exploring
>switches to taking a lot of melee.

  Teleportitis, Teleport control (at XL:17) and the spell of magic
mapping means much less melee below the Castle.  Add in skilled+ spell
of detect monster and there's almost no melee.

  And even lack of space doesn't mean you should give up casting attack
spells.  Using FoD or XL:30 magic missile generally gets rid of
dangerous monsters much faster than using weapons.


>With manna early on, it is important to watch your level.  Blast
>away a spell or two, switch to projectiles, finish with melee.  Try
>not to run completely out of either manna or daggers when possible.
>But putting on body armor switches that to trying a blast or two
>with spells that might or might not work while the distance is still
>large enough to be able to thorw daggers whether the spells
>succeeded or failed.  


  Depends on both the spell and the body armor.  Remember, even an XL:1
Wizard wearing mithril can cast the spell of magic missile with only 10%
failure rate.

  Even there, not casting attack spells doesn't mean no spell casting at
all.  Many spells are just as good when cast "off-line."  So casting
unreliable spells that you don't need in combat seems like a waste of
mana.  Mana that could be put to use in non-attack spells.

  Yes, this is complicated.  Wizard is not a class for the hard of
thinking.


